<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The artwork is full-bleed, so it is the background layer and the foreground is empty.

    An adaptive icon draws a 108dp canvas of which only the central 72dp is guaranteed to survive
    the launcher's mask; the outer 18dp on each side is cropped, and shifted for parallax. Artwork
    placed in the foreground would be masked *over* the background, showing a ring of whatever
    colour sat behind it. Putting it in the background instead means the mask simply trims the
    edges of the picture, which is what a picture wants.

    There is deliberately no <monochrome>: a themed icon has to read as a single-colour stencil,
    and flattening this illustration into one would produce an unrecognisable blob. Without the
    element, launchers fall back to the full-colour icon.
-->
<adaptive-icon xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <background android:drawable="@mipmap/ic_launcher_bg" />
    <foreground android:drawable="@drawable/ic_launcher_foreground" />
</adaptive-icon>
